{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTLV6DBt6RPpo5FrPhiS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"{\"recommendations\":[{\"key\":\"r1\",\"kind\":\"fact\",\"operation\":\"add\",\"target\":{\"kind\":\"newSection\",\"heading\":\"Commands\"},\"rationale\":\"No CLAUDE.md exists. The package scripts are the main entry points for building, linting and testing, and an agent needs them first.\",\"support\":[\"F-1\",\"F-2\",\"F-3\",\"F-4\",\"F-7\"],\"references\":[{\"kind\":\"command\",\"value\":\"pnpm build\",\"support\":\"F-1\"},{\"kind\":\"command\",\"value\":\"pnpm dev\",\"support\":\"F-2\"},{\"kind\":\"command\",\"value\":\"pnpm lint\",\"support\":\"F-3\"},{\"kind\":\"command\",\"value\":\"pnpm lint:fix\",\"support\":\"F-4\"},{\"kind\":\"command\",\"value\":\"pnpm test\",\"support\":\"F-7\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"package.json\",\"support\":\"F-1\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"src/index.ts\",\"support\":\"F-1\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"src\",\"support\":\"F-3\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"test\",\"support\":\"F-3\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"examples\",\"support\":\"F-3\"}],\"scope\":{\"kind\":\"repository\"},\"content\":\"The scripts are defined in `package.json`:\\n\\n- `pnpm build` builds the library from `src/index.ts` with `obuild`.\\n- `pnpm dev` runs Vitest.\\n- `pnpm lint` runs ESLint and a Prettier check over `src`, `test` and `examples`; `pnpm lint:fix` applies the fixes.\\n- `pnpm test` runs `pnpm lint` and then the Vitest suite with coverage.\"},{\"key\":\"r2\",\"kind\":\"fact\",\"operation\":\"add\",\"target\":{\"kind\":\"newSection\",\"heading\":\"Tooling\"},\"rationale\":\"Describes the lint setup and the autofix workflow, so an agent knows lint fixes are also applied automatically in CI.\",\"support\":[\"F-10\",\"F-11\",\"F-13\"],\"references\":[{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"eslint.config.mjs\",\"support\":\"F-10\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\".github/workflows/autofix.yml\",\"support\":\"F-11\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"vitest.config.ts\",\"support\":\"F-13\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"src\",\"support\":\"F-13\"}],\"scope\":{\"kind\":\"repository\"},\"content\":\"Linting uses `eslint-config-unjs` via `eslint.config.mjs`, with some rules turned off there.\\n\\nThe `.github/workflows/autofix.yml` workflow runs the `lint:fix` script on pull requests and pushes to `main` and commits the results.\\n\\nTest coverage in `vitest.config.ts` is restricted to `src`.\"},{\"key\":\"r3\",\"kind\":\"policy\",\"operation\":\"add\",\"target\":{\"kind\":\"newSection\",\"heading\":\"Code conventions\"},\"rationale\":\"The developer confirmed explicit `.ts` extensions are required for relative imports in src (D-4); tsconfig enables this.\",\"support\":[\"D-4\",\"F-9\"],\"references\":[{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"src\",\"support\":\"F-9\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"tsconfig.json\",\"support\":\"F-9\"}],\"scope\":{\"kind\":\"paths\",\"paths\":[\"src\"]},\"content\":\"Relative imports in `src` must use explicit `.ts` extensions; `tsconfig.json` enables this with `allowImportingTsExtensions` and `NodeNext` module resolution.\"},{\"key\":\"r4\",\"kind\":\"policy\",\"operation\":\"add\",\"target\":{\"kind\":\"newSection\",\"heading\":\"Behavior notes\"},\"rationale\":\"The developer decided the code is right that DELETE is a payload method and the README should be updated (D-1), resolving the README/code mismatch.\",\"support\":[\"D-1\"],\"references\":[],\"scope\":{\"kind\":\"repository\"},\"content\":\"Treat `DELETE` as a payload method, as the code does: with a body it gets JSON serialization and the default JSON headers. The README's list of PUT, PATCH and POST is out of date and should be updated to include it.\"},{\"key\":\"r5\",\"kind\":\"policy\",\"operation\":\"add\",\"target\":{\"kind\":\"newSection\",\"heading\":\"README\"},\"rationale\":\"The developer decided README generated sections should be regenerated with automd after README-affecting changes (D-2); automd is a devDependency and the README uses its markers.\",\"support\":[\"D-2\",\"F-17\"],\"references\":[{\"kind\":\"path\",\"value\":\"README.md\",\"support\":\"F-17\"}],\"scope\":{\"kind\":\"paths\",\"paths\":[\"README.md\"]},\"content\":\"`README.md` has sections generated between `automd` markers. After changes that affect the README, regenerate them with `automd` rather than editing them by hand.\"}],\"heldBack\":[{\"topic\":\"Tests import the library from `../src/index.ts` while examples import from the `ofetch` package name\",\"blockedBy\":[\"Q-6\"]},{\"topic\":\"Whether pnpm is required for development\",\"blockedBy\":[\"Q-7\"]}]}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9566,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4459,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2807},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}